  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_004 (RNA-only, PCA-2000, multiprofile, avgpool) achieves 0.591 accuracy, while both image-only models (resnet50: 0.328, ViT-L: 0.332) are far weaker, indicating RNA dominates the signal. The central question for this multimodal profiling study is whether fusing the weak image signal with the strong RNA signal improves or degrades performance. config_033 keeps the RNA side identical to config_004 (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) and adds only resnet50 with simple concat fusion, isolating the effect of adding the image modality. This is the most informative next step because it directly answers whether multimodal fusion is worthwhile before investing experiments in more complex fusion (weighted, transformer) or alternative encoders. If it helps, we exploit by trying better fusion; if it hurts, we redirect budget toward RNA-side improvements (aggregation, encoder choice)."
}

